          "source_ids": [
            "sections.0",
            "sections.1"
          ],
          "text": "You came into hospital because of a low mood that had been getting worse over 6 weeks. You were also having thoughts of suicide, including thoughts of overdose. The team found you were having a depressive episode with active suicidal ideation. They also noted that a recent relationship breakdown and work stress had played a part."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "The team assessed you and found no psychotic features. By Day 3, your sleep had improved a little and your suicidal thoughts had become less intense. By Day 5, your mood was improving and the suicidal thoughts were fleeting and passive, with no intent, and you were thinking about the future.\n\nDuring your stay:\n- An antidepressant (sertraline) was started on Day 3, 20/05.\n- You were given information about your condition (psychoeducation).\n- A safety plan was completed with you.\n- The team reviewed you on Day 5 and agreed you were ready to go home with early follow-up and a crisis line."
        },
        {
